---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Tracelane vs LangSmith Engine — pre-flight policy vs post-failure clustering">
  {/* ===== Hero ===== */}
  <section class="relative container overflow-hidden py-24 sm:py-32">
    <div
      class="glow glow-teal"
      style="width:600px;height:440px;left:50%;top:-60px;transform:translateX(-50%)"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-[2]">
      <p class="text-fg-subtle mb-8 font-mono text-sm tracking-wide lowercase">
        tracelane vs langsmith engine
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-fg max-w-4xl text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl"
      >
        Flag failures pre-flight, or <span class="grad-text">cluster them after.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-fg-muted mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed sm:text-xl">
        LangSmith Engine (May 13, 2026) clusters production failures after they happen, files pull
        requests, and bills against the LangSmith plan. Tracelane flags failure classes inline at
        the gateway, sub-50ms target, before the call reaches the provider. Different layer.
        Different commercial posture.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== TL;DR ===== */}
  <section class="border-border container border-t py-16">
    <p class="text-pop mb-4 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase">tl;dr</p>
    <ul class="text-fg-muted max-w-3xl space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>— LangSmith Engine is reactive: triage after failure has shipped.</li>
      <li>
        — Tracelane is pre-flight: flag the failure class inline at the gateway, sub-50ms target.
      </li>
      <li>
        — Engine is locked to the LangSmith trace surface and LangChain-managed inference keys per
        ToS. Tracelane is neutral OTel ingest with BYOK 0% markup across 30+ providers.
      </li>
      <li>
        — Engine adds value on top of an existing LangSmith deployment. Tracelane replaces LiteLLM +
        Helicone/Langfuse + a custom guardrail layer with one Rust binary.
      </li>
      <li>— Both are useful. They sit at different layers of the agent reliability stack.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Capability matrix ===== */}
  <section class="border-border container border-t py-24">
    <h2 class="text-fg text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Capability comparison.</h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Based on the LangSmith Engine launch announcement (May 13, 2026) and LangChain documentation.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-border-strong border-b">
            <th class="text-fg-dim py-4 pr-6 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase"
              >capability</th
            >
            <th class="text-fg-dim py-4 pr-6 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase"
              >tracelane v1</th
            >
            <th class="text-fg-dim py-4 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase"
              >langsmith engine</th
            >
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-fg-muted">
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Failure handling timing</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">Pre-flight inline at gateway, sub-50ms target</td>
            <td class="py-4">Post-failure clustering, async triage</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">LLM provider lock-in</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">None — 30+ providers, BYOK 0% markup</td>
            <td class="py-4">LangChain-managed inference keys per ToS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Trace surface</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">OTel GenAI semconv, neutral ingest</td>
            <td class="py-4">LangSmith proprietary trace format</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">License</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">Apache 2.0 core / Tracelane Enterprise / CC0 spec</td>
            <td class="py-4">Closed-source SaaS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Self-host path</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">Docker Compose, Helm, single small VPS</td>
            <td class="py-4">Hosted only (LangSmith Cloud / Enterprise)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Audit log integrity</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6"
              >SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed Merkle root, offline-verifiable</td
            >
            <td class="py-4">Application-layer trace storage; no cryptographic chain</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">EU AI Act Article 12 export pack</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">$999/mo add-on, available at V1</td>
            <td class="py-4">Not in launch announcement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-border border-b">
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Gateway included</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">Yes — Rust gateway, 30+ providers</td>
            <td class="py-4">No — assumes you bring your own (or LangChain's)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-fg py-4 pr-6">Commercial model</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-6">Open-core + usage-based hosted, MoR via Polar.sh</td>
            <td class="py-4">LangSmith plan add-on (Developer/Plus/Enterprise)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== When to choose which ===== */}
  <section class="border-border container border-t py-24">
    <h2 class="text-fg text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">When to choose which.</h2>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="border-border bg-bg-elevated rounded-lg border p-8">
        <p class="text-pop mb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase">choose tracelane if</p>
        <ul class="text-fg-muted space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li>— You want failures flagged pre-flight, not just triaged after</li>
          <li>— You need BYOK 0% markup across multiple providers</li>
          <li>— You need neutral OTel ingest, not a proprietary trace surface</li>
          <li>— You need a tamper-evident audit ledger for EU AI Act / DPDP / HIPAA</li>
          <li>— You want Apache 2.0 core with a self-host path</li>
          <li>— You don't already run LangSmith and don't want to adopt it just to get Engine</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="border-border bg-bg-elevated rounded-lg border p-8">
        <p class="text-fg-dim mb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider lowercase">
          choose langsmith engine if
        </p>
        <ul class="text-fg-muted space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li>— You already run LangSmith and your traces are there</li>
          <li>— You're committed to LangChain-managed inference keys</li>
          <li>— Post-failure clustering and PR drafting is your priority workflow</li>
          <li>— You don't need a tamper-evident audit ledger</li>
          <li>— You're not regulated under EU AI Act Annex III</li>
          <li>— A closed-source hosted SaaS is acceptable in your procurement review</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-12 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
      These tools are not mutually exclusive at the architectural layer. Tracelane sits at the
      gateway and trace-ingest layer; Engine sits on top of an existing trace store. Some teams will
      run both — Tracelane to flag failures pre-flight and produce the audit ledger, LangSmith
      Engine to cluster the failures that escape and draft fixes.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ===== CTA ===== */}
  <section class="border-border container border-t py-24">
    <h2 class="text-fg text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      Tracelane V1 — coming soon.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-fg-muted mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Open core. Apache 2.0. Self-host or use the free hosted tier.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row">
      <a href="/#notify" class="btn-primary">Get the launch email</a>
      <a href="/" class="btn-secondary">Back to Home →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
